id: energy-synchronize
name: Energy Synchronize
type: standard
actionCost: 2
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
usageLimit: 1/encounter
# A Special Maneuver: open where an effect grants it (`allow maneuver.energy-synchronize;` - which effect does, the user is finding).
# Your targeted Ally - or the one who made you theirs, answering - your Linked Character till the Encounter ends (an actor flag,
# fusion-of-ki.mjs postSync). Their answer is a button on its card for whoever plays them: 2 Standard Actions, then this
# Maneuver out of sequence (answerSync). Both made each other theirs: the Fusion of Ki Special State for both, carried out by the
# GM, who may change both (chat.mjs requestKiFusion).
special: true
energySync: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Target an Ally: your Linked Character until the end of the Combat Encounter. Once both of you have used it on each other, the
  two of you enter the Fusion of Ki Special State.
text: >
  Energy Synchronize Maneuver [1/Encounter]: You match and combine your life energy with a partner, allowing you to share your power.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 2 Actions
  –Minions: N/A
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Ally; they become your Linked Character until the end of the Combat Encounter. In response, your Linked
  Character can spend 2 Standard Actions to use the Energy Synchronize Maneuver if they have access to it as an Out-of-Sequence
  Maneuver. Once both you and your Ally have used the Energy Synchronize Maneuver with each other as your Linked Characters, the
  two of you enter the Fusion of Ki Special State for 3 Combat Rounds or until the Linked Ki Points are reduced to 0.
